# YouTube Content Creation Pipeline

Lux provides transport-neutral helpers for turning a YouTube content brief into
a production-ready plan: script, edits, thumbnail, metadata, playlist placement,
localization, repurposing, and A/B testing.

## Content Brief

```elixir
alias Lux.Integrations.YouTube.ContentPipeline

brief = %{
  topic: "Build AI agents with Elixir",
  audience: "developers",
  goal: "ship reliable automations",
  key_points: ["Define the workflow", "Add tests", "Deploy safely"],
  summary: "A practical production workflow.",
  keywords: ["Elixir", "AI Agents", "Automation"],
  languages: ["es", "zh"],
  pillar: "Agent Engineering",
  title: "Build AI agents with Elixir"
}
```

## Script Outline

```elixir
ContentPipeline.script_outline(brief)
```

## Editing Suggestions

```elixir
ContentPipeline.editing_suggestions(%{
  intro_seconds: 30,
  estimated_minutes: 8,
  sections: [%{}, %{}, %{}],
  needs_visual_examples: true
})
```

## Thumbnail Brief

```elixir
ContentPipeline.thumbnail_brief(brief)
```

## Metadata Plan

```elixir
ContentPipeline.metadata_plan(brief)
```

The metadata plan includes title, description, normalized tags, cards, and end
screen defaults.

## Playlist and Localization

```elixir
ContentPipeline.playlist_plan(brief)
ContentPipeline.localization_tasks(brief)
```

## Repurposing

```elixir
ContentPipeline.repurposing_ideas(brief)
```

## A/B Testing

```elixir
ContentPipeline.ab_test_plan(%{
  title: "Build AI agents with Elixir",
  title_b: "Reliable Elixir agents in production",
  thumbnail_a: "thumb-a",
  thumbnail_b: "thumb-b"
})
```

## Full Pipeline

```elixir
ContentPipeline.pipeline(brief)
```

Use the full pipeline output as a handoff to agents, editors, schedulers, or
metadata update tools.
